5
00:01:08,360 --> 00:01:10,819
<i>Aku tak tahu bagaimana
ada orang yang bisa.</i>

6
00:01:12,833 --> 00:01:14,334
<i>Terutama ini...</i>

7
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,612
<i>75% dunia, mungkin lebih.</i>

8
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:31,029
{\an8}<font color="#ffe4ac">FRAGMEN MENGHANCURKAN FLORIDA TENGAH</font>

9
00:01:26,712 --> 00:01:28,129
<i>Kita masih belum tahu pasti.</i>

10
00:01:29,506 --> 00:01:31,049
<i>Hilang.</i>

11
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:40,459
<i>Lima tahun sejak tumbukan,</i>

12
00:01:40,559 --> 00:01:43,212
<i>namun Clarke
belum selesai dengan kita.</i>

13
00:01:43,312 --> 00:01:46,006
<i>Fragmen tersangkut di orbit,</i>

14
00:01:46,106 --> 00:01:48,441
<i>menghujani tanpa peringatan.</i>

15
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,220
<i>Kami mencoba membangun kembali,</i>

16
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,113
<i>tapi dunia belum siap.</i>

17
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:56,783
<i>Memaksa kami kembali ke dalam.</i>

18
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:01,329
<i>Radiasi menghantam
dengan cara berbeda di tiap tempat.</i>

19
00:02:01,997 --> 00:02:04,143
<i>Sebagian besar hangus.</i>

20
00:02:04,244 --> 00:02:08,670
<i>Yang lain, entah kenapa,
tetap hijau.</i>

21
00:02:10,836 --> 00:02:14,591
<i>Hidup, menemukan jalan
di tengah kontaminasi.</i>

22
00:02:42,763 --> 00:02:44,622
<i>Bunker kami masih bertahan.</i>

23
00:02:47,256 --> 00:02:48,918
<i>Kami lakukan yang terbaik.</i>

24
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:53,923
<i>Tak mudah hidup di bawah tanah.</i>

25
00:02:55,967 --> 00:02:58,178
<i>Namun kami mencari bahagia
sebisa mungkin.</i>

26
00:03:00,883 --> 00:03:01,931
<i>Bersama.</i>

27
00:03:09,610 --> 00:03:13,090
<font color="#c7fffa">GREENLAND</font>

28
00:03:13,191 --> 00:03:18,871
<font color="#c7fffa">GREENLAND: MIGRASI</font>

29
00:03:31,289 --> 00:03:33,421
Cek mikrofon.
Satu, dua. Satu, dua.

30
00:03:36,049 --> 00:03:37,634
<i>Jelas terdengar, John.</i>

31
00:03:39,511 --> 00:03:41,720
Tahu apa yang kupikirkan
saat bangun tadi?

32
00:03:43,682 --> 00:03:45,183
<i>Katakanlah.</i>

33
00:03:46,435 --> 00:03:48,587
Biskuit dan kuah daging.

34
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:50,881
<i>Itu pasti enak.</i>

35
00:03:50,981 --> 00:03:53,483
<i>Aku rela menukar lengan kiriku
demi secangkir kopi layak.</i>

36
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,678
Peckman's Diner
membuat yang terbaik.

37
00:03:56,778 --> 00:03:58,972
Di seberang Piedmont Park.

38
00:03:59,072 --> 00:04:01,433
Jalan kaki menuju
konser musim panas.

39
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:03,785
Langit biru, rumput, orang-orang.

40
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:05,646
Bir.

41
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,064
<i>Terdengar seperti surga.</i>

42
00:04:07,164 --> 00:04:08,665
Memang begitu.

43
00:04:11,283 --> 00:04:14,237
Astaga...
Retakan baru terbuka lagi.

44
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:15,947
<i>Lava lagi?</i>

45
00:04:16,343 --> 00:04:18,258
Ya, dan makin membesar.

46
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:46,286
Baiklah, sepertinya kita punya
beberapa sekoci.

47
00:04:50,403 --> 00:04:51,874
Dan satu kapal hantu lagi.

48
00:04:52,556 --> 00:04:54,152
Sebuah kapal perusak.

49
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:56,988
<i>Bagus.
Hari ini merasa beruntung?</i>

50
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:58,955
Selalu. Aku mulai dari sekoci dulu,

51
00:04:59,056 --> 00:05:00,075
Lihat apa yang ada.

52
00:05:00,470 --> 00:05:01,463
<i>Semoga beruntung di luar sana.</i>

53
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:21,779
Menuju kapal perusak.

54
00:05:26,163 --> 00:05:28,156
<i>Kami melihat badai tekanan
membangun di lepas pantai,</i>

55
00:05:28,257 --> 00:05:30,248
<i>tapi sepertinya
kau masih punya sedikit waktu.</i>

56
00:05:30,349 --> 00:05:32,010
Aku takkan berlama-lama.

57
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,353
Jackpot.

58
00:06:02,023 --> 00:06:03,363
Memasuki ruang kendali.

59
00:06:08,343 --> 00:06:10,370
Aku temukan sesuatu lagi.

60
00:06:11,130 --> 00:06:12,372
<i>Apa itu, John?</i>

61
00:06:14,743 --> 00:06:15,792
Kru kapal.

62
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:18,628
<i>Sial.</i>

63
00:06:47,303 --> 00:06:49,200
Oh, betapa indahnya.

64
00:06:51,496 --> 00:06:52,850
<i>John...</i>

65
00:06:54,430 --> 00:06:58,110
<i>John, kau dengar aku?
John, kau dengar aku?</i>

66
00:06:58,211 --> 00:07:00,153
<i>Badai itu berbelok langsung ke arahmu.</i>

67
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,322
<i>Kau harus segera keluar
dan kembali ke sini!</i>

68
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:03,563
Dalam perjalanan.

69
00:07:04,563 --> 00:07:07,160
Keluar dari kapal sekarang.
Berapa waktu yang kupunya?

70
00:07:07,450 --> 00:07:08,970
<i>Tak ada. Itu tepat di atasmu.</i>

71
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:22,263
Ayo...

72
00:07:24,076 --> 00:07:26,279
Aku masih di depan,
tapi badai makin mendekat.

73
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:34,723
Sial, markas...
Yang ini datang terlalu cepat!

74
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:39,818
<i>John! John, kau di mana?</i>

75
00:07:40,296 --> 00:07:42,253
Aku bergerak secepat yang kubisa!

76
00:07:47,243 --> 00:07:48,926
Buka terowongan timur!

77
00:07:50,679 --> 00:07:52,170
Buka pintunya!

78
00:07:53,323 --> 00:07:55,264
Buka pintu! Cepat buka!

79
00:08:00,070 --> 00:08:01,423
<i>Badai terlalu dekat!</i>

80
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,089
<i>Kita harus menutup pintu ledak, John!</i>

81
00:08:03,190 --> 00:08:04,399
Aku bisa masuk!

82
00:08:11,436 --> 00:08:12,684
Tutup, tutup, tutup!

83
00:08:12,784 --> 00:08:14,060
Cepat, cepat, cepat!

84
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,828
<i>John, kau sudah masuk?</i>

85
00:08:22,909 --> 00:08:32,103
{\an8}<font color="#ffe4ac">PANGKALAN UDARA THULE
STASIUN GREENLAND</font>

86
00:08:48,783 --> 00:08:50,180
<i>Bucharest, Rumania.</i>

87
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,140
<i>Kota hancur oleh gempa bumi.</i>

88
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,517
<i>Kami terjebak di bawah...</i>

89
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:55,996
<i>Mumbai, India.</i>

90
00:08:56,097 --> 00:08:58,104
<i>Air asin masih terus naik cepat.</i>

91
00:08:58,423 --> 00:09:00,148
FEMA merencanakan dua tahun.

92
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,376
Kami paksa sumber daya
hingga lima tahun.

93
00:09:02,477 --> 00:09:04,152
Jadi kita hampir kehabisan?

94
00:09:04,643 --> 00:09:07,364
Ya. Kita makin dekat batas.

95
00:09:07,950 --> 00:09:12,070
Semoga setahun lagi
kita sudah di luar menanam.

96
00:09:14,354 --> 00:09:17,340
{\an8}<font color="#ffe4ac">JOHN KEMBALI DENGAN SELAMAT</font>

97
00:09:13,254 --> 00:09:16,240
Kami mencatat penurunan 4%

98
00:09:16,347 --> 00:09:19,363
coulomb per kilogram
dalam tiga bulan terakhir.

99
00:09:19,464 --> 00:09:22,175
Kami masih tak bisa memprediksi
kapan levelnya aman lagi, tapi...

100
00:09:22,276 --> 00:09:24,172
- Tapi ada perbaikan, kan?
- Ya.

101
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,007
Meski itu lebih banyak
di lepas pantai.

102
00:09:26,107 --> 00:09:28,969
Ya. Semoga angin akhirnya
membersihkan radiasi.

103
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:30,929
Tidak, itu bukan cara kerjanya.

104
00:09:31,470 --> 00:09:33,582
Paparan radiasi terus-menerus,

105
00:09:33,683 --> 00:09:37,519
meski pada level rendah
tetap berujung fatal.

106
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:39,604
Kita harus membahas
rencana darurat.

107
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:41,523
Baik, ya. Um...

108
00:09:42,156 --> 00:09:45,251
Kanada, dan sebagian besar AS, lenyap.

109
00:09:45,750 --> 00:09:47,378
Islandia, lenyap.

110
00:09:47,763 --> 00:09:49,210
Eropa Barat?

111
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,335
Ada laporan badai lebih
sedikit di sana, benar?

112
00:09:52,436 --> 00:09:53,843
- Ya.
- Tapi apakah udaranya aman?

113
00:09:55,176 --> 00:09:56,236
Lebih aman daripada di sini.

114
00:09:56,337 --> 00:09:59,791
Bukankah tadi kita bilang
mati perlahan tetaplah mati?

115
00:10:00,150 --> 00:10:02,002
Maksudku, benar kan, Dr. Amina?

116
00:10:02,523 --> 00:10:05,063
- Bukankah sama saja di sana?
- Ya.

117
00:10:08,096 --> 00:10:10,610
Dr. Amina, apa kabar terbaru
tentang kawah itu?

118
00:10:14,072 --> 00:10:17,767
Rekan-rekanku di stasiun lain
juga berteori hal yang sama.

119
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,728
Dan aku sudah jalankan
perhitunganku sendiri.

120
00:10:19,828 --> 00:10:21,210
Kita tak bisa menjelaskan sepenuhnya,

121
00:10:21,311 --> 00:10:24,190
tapi tampaknya ukuran
dan bentuk dinding kawah

122
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,776
mencegah badai radioaktif terbentuk.

123
00:10:26,876 --> 00:10:28,570
Ditambah dengan kedalamannya

124
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:30,196
itulah yang menjadikannya
zona aman.

125
00:10:30,296 --> 00:10:31,072
Kami percaya itu yang menjaga

126
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:33,036
agar udara tercemar
tak masuk ke dalam.

127
00:10:33,137 --> 00:10:35,785
Tapi, Dr. Amina, meski itu nyata,

128
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,896
lokasinya di Prancis Selatan.

129
00:10:38,513 --> 00:10:40,248
Bagaimana tepatnya
kita bisa sampai ke sana?

130
00:10:40,348 --> 00:10:42,042
Ada laporan pertempuran,

131
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:44,210
pemberontakan, perang sipil.

132
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,686
Eropa kacau balau.

133
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:50,223
Tolonglah...
Mari tetap berpegang pada kenyataan.

134
00:10:55,572 --> 00:10:58,224
<i>Perhatian warga,
ini pengingat harian kalian</i>

135
00:10:58,324 --> 00:10:59,768
<i>untuk melaporkan setiap kerusakan
filtrasi udara...</i>

136
00:10:59,868 --> 00:11:01,811
<i>Harap hemat dengan cermat
dan hanya...</i>

137
00:11:01,911 --> 00:11:04,664
<i>Ada orang di sini
yang bilang ini normal baru.</i>

138
00:11:05,790 --> 00:11:07,458
Yah, kita sudah...

139
00:11:07,959 --> 00:11:09,986
- lima tahun sekarang?
- Mmm-hmm.

140
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,671
Jadi ini bukan hal baru.

141
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:14,115
Dan jelas bukan normal.

142
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:16,493
Kau tahu,
bukan kebetulan kalau ada

143
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:17,994
dua kali lebih banyak terapis dipilih

144
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,413
dibandingkan ahli bedah.

145
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:23,625
Orang-orang menghadapi
trauma luar biasa.

146
00:11:23,725 --> 00:11:25,585
Kenapa semua orang
berpura-pura tidak, ya?

147
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:26,762
- Kau juga?
- Berpurapura?

148
00:11:26,863 --> 00:11:28,437
Mmm-hmm.

149
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:31,148
Kadang-kadang.

150
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:33,950
Mungkin kau harus berhenti.

151
00:11:34,051 --> 00:11:35,845
Yah, mungkin kau bisa rekomendasikan
terapis bagus

152
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,238
yang bisa membantuku soal itu.

153
00:11:37,767 --> 00:11:38,897
Punyaku cukup bagus.

154
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,706
Jadi, uh...

155
00:11:48,291 --> 00:11:50,960
Allison, Nathan, bagaimana mereka?

156
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,113
Mereka bertahan.

157
00:11:53,213 --> 00:11:54,714
Kupikir... semoga begitu.

158
00:11:56,633 --> 00:11:59,552
Keterbukaan itu penting. Uh...

159
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:03,180
Yah, mereka cukup terbuka
padaku.

160
00:12:04,390 --> 00:12:05,891
Maksudku sebaliknya.

161
00:12:21,157 --> 00:12:22,837
Sepertinya belakangan
lebih sering terjadi.

162
00:12:24,327 --> 00:12:26,723
Lempeng tektonik bergerak lagi.

163
00:12:27,249 --> 00:12:29,643
Memicu banyak aktivitas
di wilayah ini.

164
00:12:29,744 --> 00:12:31,776
Bunker ini selamat dari Clarke.

165
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,436
Ia akan selamat dari gempa.

166
00:12:33,537 --> 00:12:35,923
Ada satu hal lagi
yang harus kita bahas.

167
00:12:36,024 --> 00:12:38,908
Sinyal darurat
yang kita terima dari luar.

168
00:12:39,008 --> 00:12:41,077
Kita tak mampu memberi makan
50 mulut tambahan.

169
00:12:41,177 --> 00:12:43,121
Lima saja tak sanggup.

170
00:12:43,221 --> 00:12:44,455
Aku tahu,
tapi orang-orang itu hidup

171
00:12:44,555 --> 00:12:46,163
di gua dan terowongan tambang.

172
00:12:46,264 --> 00:12:48,585
Ya, dan kita tak tahu
apakah mereka membawa penyakit

173
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:50,576
atau berapa banyak radiasi
yang mereka serap.

174
00:12:51,187 --> 00:12:53,522
Baiklah. Jadi kita biarkan
mereka mati.

175
00:12:55,643 --> 00:12:58,887
Kita bilang pada mereka
bahwa saat ini kita

176
00:12:58,987 --> 00:13:00,446
tak dalam posisi untuk membantu.

177
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:03,136
- Ya?
- Tidak.

178
00:13:03,237 --> 00:13:05,727
Kita putuskan lewat suara
seperti biasa.

179
00:13:05,827 --> 00:13:08,120
Usulan mengirim tim penyelamat?

180
00:13:09,396 --> 00:13:10,581
Aku setuju.

181
00:13:21,623 --> 00:13:22,660
Jenderal...

182
00:13:22,760 --> 00:13:24,412
Keputusan tetap.

183
00:13:24,703 --> 00:13:27,223
Kita kirim Snowcat besok.

184
00:13:28,630 --> 00:13:31,336
Dan saat kita menatap langit utara,

185
00:13:31,437 --> 00:13:33,763
rasi bintang apa ini?

186
00:13:34,263 --> 00:13:36,816
- Gemini?
- Tidak. Bukan Gemini.

187
00:13:37,563 --> 00:13:38,776
Nathan?

188
00:13:40,016 --> 00:13:42,138
Oh, um, itu Cassiopeia.

189
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,930
Kau bisa tahu dari bentuk W-nya.

190
00:13:44,869 --> 00:13:47,310
Kenapa kita harus
belajar banyak soal bintang?

191
00:13:47,410 --> 00:13:50,521
Yah, mungkin seharusnya dulu kita
lebih memperhatikan mereka.

192
00:13:50,776 --> 00:13:52,832
Clarke bukan bintang, itu komet.

193
00:13:53,041 --> 00:13:54,025
Masih komet.

194
00:13:54,125 --> 00:13:55,843
Tapi sudah menghantam bumi.

195
00:13:56,223 --> 00:13:57,542
Bagian terbesarnya memang,

196
00:13:57,643 --> 00:14:00,573
tapi serpihan kecil yang tidak,

197
00:14:00,673 --> 00:14:03,576
terjebak dalam gravitasi kita.

198
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:07,054
Menciptakan apa yang disebut
cincin hantu.

199
00:14:33,330 --> 00:14:35,233
Lars, apa ini?

200
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:37,610
Apa? Ini rock and roll klasik.

201
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:42,365
Kalau maksudmu rock klasik,
ini bukan itu.

202
00:14:42,465 --> 00:14:45,910
Berikan aku The Stones,
The Allman Brothers...

203
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:49,346
Michael McDonald,
itu baru rock klasik.

204
00:14:50,348 --> 00:14:52,850
Billy Ocean. Juga lumayan keren.

205
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:58,312
Putar saja katupnya sekarang.

206
00:15:07,698 --> 00:15:10,326
Ayo, Sayang. Ini dia!

207
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:18,735
Whoo! Kita kembali berfungsi!

208
00:15:18,835 --> 00:15:19,936
Bagus!

209
00:15:21,656 --> 00:15:22,922
Kita bisa minum air lagi.

210
00:15:25,633 --> 00:15:26,926
Ibu...

211
00:15:28,103 --> 00:15:29,162
Ibu, aku bisa jelaskan.

212
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:30,913
Nathan, Ibu tak mau dengar!

213
00:15:31,013 --> 00:15:33,029
